  "text": "Fasten something so it stays in place.\n\nThink about how they secured the cloth\n\nContinuing to be true up to this time.\n\nForming an idea without being certain.\n\nFrom one side or opening to the other.\n\nPaid attention to what could be heard.\n\nThe end of a narrow or pointed object.\n\nLooking at this word in your sentence…\n\nTalk with Rina about what happens next\n\nGrandma is beside the planting circle.\n\nM0 136q62-35 124-16 123-43 236 7v73H0Z\n\nAmusing; likely to make someone laugh.\n\nFitted firmly into its intended place.\n\nAn amount or number that is not exact.\n\nPut something into its intended place.\n\nExtended as far as needed or possible.\n\nPressed gently to make a surface flat.\n\nCorrect or suitable in this situation.\n\nOpened something that had been folded.\n\nOffer an idea for someone to consider.\n\nYour message is ready to tell Grandma.\n\ng-reading-tools g-conversation-reading\n\nThe ending is your suggested wording.\n\nThe Garden Adventure · Evidence Quest\n\nUnits of language that carry meaning.\n\nMaking food such as bread in an oven.\n\nOn the opposite side of the crossing.\n\nFastened so something stays in place.\n\nConnect things so they stay together.\n\nSTORIES & INVENTIONS MADE BY CHILDREN\n\nHold, move or take care of something.\n\nFeedback on these selected words only\n\nWould you like help with your ending?\n\nPass something around another object.\n\nPip can't reach that place from here.\n\nUsing the mind to consider something.\n\nA piece of furniture with a flat top.\n\nPlans about what will happen and how.\n\nNoticed sound or listened to someone.\n\nMara: has agreed to this arrangement.\n\nMoved something slowly and carefully.\n\nDeciding what to do and how to do it.\n\nReading help · Your preview is paused\n\nAsked a business to supply something.\n\nOpening something out over a surface.",
